  {
    "repo": "stm32h7xx-hal-driver",
    "pr_number": 48,
    "title": "fix the bug that the spi suspend flag is not cleared",
    "state": "closed",
    "merged": false,
    "draft": false,
    "author": "huoxingdawang",
    "labels": [
      "enhancement",
      "wontfix",
      "hal"
    ],
    "created_at": "2024-03-11T16:20:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-18T09:07:40Z",
    "closed_at": "2024-03-15T11:36:35Z",
    "merged_at": null,
    "body": "This PR fix the issue #47 .\r\n\r\nThe thing is that the SPI master in the rx only mode won't wait the CPU to get data from the fifo. So if a interrupt occured during the `HAL_SPI_Receive`, data will lose and the `while (hspi->RxXferCount > 0UL)` will nerver exit, which will then cause a timeout error.\r\n\r\nThere is actually a bit `MASRX` designed for the SPI mater to wait CPU, but after the CPU get data, the SUSP flag need to be cleared in order to start the receive according to the reference manual.\r\n\r\nWithout clearing the susp bit, the SPI master won't receive data anymore, which will also cause a timeout.  Very much like the case without setting MASRX.\r\n\r\nThis PR fixed this bug by adding codes to clear the susp flag in `HAL_SPI_Receive`. After my testing, I think it works very well.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32h7xx_hal_driver/assets/34576789/9694e6d7-d29e-451a-812d-72987eca4fdc)\r\n",
    "github_url": "https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32h7xx-hal-driver/pull/48",
    "head_ref": "master",
    "base_ref": "master",
    "merge_commit_sha": "7e9f7b331f1b849ff24064e33e42b495b5bf9b31",
    "commits_count": 1,
    "review_comments_count": 0,
